# Jarvis - environment variables
#
# This file documents the variable NAMES and their defaults. It is not loaded
# automatically and there is deliberately no .env reader in the codebase: values
# come from the real process environment, so there is no dotenv parser to keep
# in sync and no chance of a stray file holding a real secret.
#
# Copy to .env only as a record of your own values, or export them directly:
#
#     export JARVIS_TOKEN="$(openssl rand -hex 32)"
#
# For the launchd plist, put the values in <key>JARVIS_TOKEN</key> under
# EnvironmentVariables.
#
# Precedence, highest first: environment -> config.yaml -> config.example.yaml
# -> built-in defaults. JARVIS_TOKEN is the one exception: it is read from the
# environment ONLY, never from YAML, so it cannot be copied into a file that
# might be shared or committed.
#
# NOTE ON SECRETS: JARVIS_TOKEN is the only protection standing between this
# API and the personal data in the store. If it is unset, every /api/* request
# is refused (fail closed) rather than allowed through.

# Bearer token required by every /api/* route:
#   Authorization: Bearer <JARVIS_TOKEN>
# No default. Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
# It must never appear in a URL; query-string tokens are rejected, because URLs
# reach access logs and Referer headers.
JARVIS_TOKEN=

# Interface to bind. Loopback only by default, and should stay that way: remote
# access is meant to arrive via Tailscale Serve proxying to 127.0.0.1, not by
# listening on a LAN or public interface.
JARVIS_HOST=127.0.0.1

# TCP port for the local server.
JARVIS_PORT=8123

# SQLite database file. Relative paths resolve against the repo root.
# Defaults to storage.db_path from the YAML config, else data/jarvis.db
JARVIS_DB_PATH=

# Append-only raw memory directory. Relative paths resolve against the repo
# root. Defaults to storage.raw_dir from the YAML config, else memory/raw
JARVIS_RAW_DIR=

# Local Ollama endpoint. Overrides llm.base_url from the YAML config.
# There is no cloud fallback: if this is unreachable, Jarvis has no model.
OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1

# Optional, manually invoked Gmail read-only integration. Supply either a
# Google Desktop OAuth client-secrets JSON file path or both client values.
# Never commit actual credentials, token files, or OAuth responses.
# JARVIS_GMAIL_CLIENT_SECRETS_FILE=
# JARVIS_GMAIL_CLIENT_ID=
# JARVIS_GMAIL_CLIENT_SECRET=
# JARVIS_GMAIL_TOKEN_FILE=data/gmail_oauth_token.json
# Optional Gmail search query (for example a recent date range).
# JARVIS_GMAIL_QUERY=
